## Summary

I implemented the **native Apple SwiftUI `ComboboxMulti` shared surface** (P4/0149) at full parity with the web source `components/forms/ComboboxMulti.tsx`, following the established codebase architecture in **10 files** (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/ComboboxMulti.{swift,Adapter,Model,Logic,Views,Listbox,Previews,strings,AdapterTests,Tests}`):

- **Faithful parity** — removable chips, filter `TextField`, dropdown that hides already‑selected rows, static **and** async (debounced, cancel‑on‑keystroke) option sources, selection cap, and every real source state: closed, loading (spinner + “Loading”), empty/“No results”, “Maximum reached”, populated + “{{count}} more — refine search” overflow, disabled, hidden‑label. A failed async load degrades to the empty branch exactly as the web `.catch` does (the source has no error/stale/offline chrome, matching sibling presentational surfaces).
- **Full keyboard model** (arrows/Home/End/Enter/Esc/Backspace/Tab), VoiceOver labels on every control, Dynamic Type + reduce‑motion, all **10 i18n keys** via the P1/S10 facade, `view.opened` telemetry, and adapter/view/a11y/strings **tests**.

**Per‑surface verification — all green** (scoped to the 10 files): swiftlint `--strict` → **0 violations**; swiftformat `--lint` → **0/9**; check‑placeholders → **0**; and it **compiles cleanly** in the normal app build (app + extensions linked).

